From 90b8828a86790213bcc9263c708e1666f2126712 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:27:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(history): send the exact --since cutoff instead of whole
 hours

`sysknife history --since <datetime>` and the MCP `sysknife_history` tool
converted the datetime into a whole-hour count with integer division, and
the daemon filtered on `now - N hours`. A cutoff 30 minutes ago became
`since_hours = 0` and matched nothing; 90 minutes ago became 1 hour and
dropped every row between 60 and 90 minutes old.

The CLI now normalises `--since` to an RFC 3339 UTC timestamp and sends it
as `since` on both the `ListJobHistory` query and the structured
`query_history` request. The store layer takes a `HistorySince` lower
bound that is either the planner's `Hours(n)` (unchanged semantics for
`query_job_history`'s `since_hours`) or an exact `Cutoff(instant)`.
SQLite compares through julianday() and Postgres through ::timestamptz,
so stored `Z`, offset and legacy `datetime('now')` rows are all compared
in UTC. Sending both `since` and `since_hours` is rejected as ambiguous.

Closes #567
